cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you build on this software, findings, or ideas, please cite this repository and the exact commit used."
type: software
title: "ExactKV: Exact refinement of a native quantized KV cache"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.1.0
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/ExactKV"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/ExactKV"
abstract: >-
  A CPU codec that recovers original BF16 cache words from native 4-bit codes
  and refinement data. Exact reconstruction passed on 21,504 real cache pages
  from three Qwen3-0.6B development prompts, but fully counted storage savings
  did not cover projected working buffers. The experiment stopped before GPU
  decoding, integrated verification, or physical-memory measurements.
keywords:
  - language models
  - KV cache
  - lossless compression
  - BF16
  - quantization
  - negative results
